# Raise an event when kapacitor fails to deliver alert mail.
#
# kapacitor queues mail and sends it in the background, so a dial or auth failure
# never reaches the alert or `kapacitor service-tests smtp` -- it is only logged to
# /var/log/kapacitor/kapacitor.log on the node that tried to send. A customer's relay
# rejected every alert mail this way and nobody knew until the outage it failed to
# report.
#
# Cron rather than a telegraf exec input: the check must not depend on the telemetry
# stack whose alerts it is guarding. alert_smtp_delivery_check is one stat and a read
# of whatever the log gained since the last run, and is a no-op on nodes without
# kapacitor.
*/2 * * * * root /usr/sbin/hex_sdk alert_smtp_delivery_check >/dev/null 2>&1
